WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.013
Blood culture contamination usually occurs when microorganisms from the skin or environment enter the sample during collection.

2
00:00:08.013 --> 00:00:09.427
Inadequate skin disinfection.

3
00:00:09.427 --> 00:00:12.726
Touching the puncture site after cleaning it.

4
00:00:12.726 --> 00:00:16.026
Collecting blood through an existing intravenous line.

5
00:00:16.026 --> 00:00:18.854
Insufficient drying time for the antiseptic.

6
00:00:18.854 --> 00:00:22.153
And failure to maintain sterile technique throughout.

7
00:00:22.153 --> 00:00:25.924
Every one of these is within your control.

